      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We describe the case of a 64-year-old woman who experienced a left renal sub-capsular hematoma following complex percutaneous coronary intervention. The hemorrhage was arrested by balloon inflation followed by coil embolization. Final thrombosis around the coil was achieved by an infusion of a small amount of thrombin."},
